{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a clear, interpretable baseline for the multimodal pipeline. config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the most standard 'vanilla' multimodal configuration: it combines both modalities, uses a learned RNA latent (scvi_n200) with a conventional CNN (resnet50), and applies the simplest aggregation (avgpool) and fusion (concat). This anchors the search at a reasonable performance level and, crucially, isolates the contribution of each design axis—subsequent experiments can then systematically upgrade the image encoder (to imagenet_vit_l), the RNA encoder (to pca_n2000 or scgpt), the aggregation (to transformer), or the fusion (to weighted) to determine which changes yield the largest gains. Starting here maximizes information gain per experiment under the 10-run budget by giving a clean reference point against which all component upgrades can be measured."
}

